] [17592186054665 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving System of Equations Graphically" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054665 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054665 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bd4dde78-84d1-5b33-a41a-9f10b24131b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Systems of Nonlinear Equations Using Graphs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054864 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a163662d-b871-5e67-90b7-3c408d42da30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186051482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054992 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ae/aee38b4fa46a403ee9517fc5a087434c8205b6553a4ebefa43be74ba7babfbc0.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x, y)$ of the following system of equations:\n${y = x + 1; y = x^{2} + 1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8c76a9c4-fcd2-5048-9771-c38b93693e80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055618 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055618 #edb/ref 1061 19145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055618 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8d314c2a-668c-507d-a140-8f47f8422fff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055618 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055619 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055619 #edb/ref 1061 19148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055619 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "487c6fc8-1141-5f82-85ea-4e560f81130f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055619 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055620 #edb/ref 1061 19149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055620 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "74edc604-916f-54b2-899e-637369c1a92d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055620 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055982 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to solve the following system of equations:\n![](images/01/01eee66dd39797b90503716f097ff604a4f339d8ea0a25ceef9b8ea7a0898ab4.svg)\n\nTo solve systems of equations *graphically*, we first draw each of the equations in the same coordinate system. Then, the solution of the system is given by the common points where the lines intersect.\n\nLet's see how this method works for the system above. To plot the functions given by the equations, we first rewrite them by making ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) the subject in each equation.\n![](images/c7/c7778dd2c82032ef68ad8221a990abe1b2bafb4e36a7a0e2640a43856be58c5a.svg) \n\nThen, we draw the lines in the same coordinate system:\n\n![](images/47/47fb02cf8bb4668b24034302fd4265ec5261f4d244cd9d9d599afeffd91d2424.png)\n\nThe lines intersect at the point ![](images/d8/d87c68d6226f4bb9ecf52ab576a5ac45c83fbb02c83edd1af04ac235dd518467.svg), which is the solution to our system.\n\n![](images/b3/b3b95135ad9a758f891280b15e8bd6f6165bf9f47a76a1c99280af02dad78911.png)\n\nWe can also use the graphical method to solve systems of equations where the corresponding functions are not straight lines. These types of systems are called **nonlinear systems**. Let's consider such an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055982 #edb/ref 1065 3407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055982 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e7d63cd6-92ea-5bb3-adc8-f9d09bf2d24d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055982 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
